 4. 🧛 When darkness falls for trick-or-treaters 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Axios analysis of NOAA solar calculations , Census Bureau. Map: Brad Jennings/Axios Most Halloween trick-or-treaters will have to start early to catch daylight. Our mapping of NOAA's astronomical sunset calculations found the sun will set before 6 p.m. in nearly a quarter of U.S. counties.

 Tonight will still bring the latest sunsets we'll get for months. Clocks will "fall back" overnight, and it'll get darker earlier across America starting tomorrow. 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 5. 🏛️ Meta builds bipartisan force 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 From left: Rep. Troy Carter (D-La.), New Orleans Saints owner/CEO Gayle Benson, Meta's Dina Powell McCormick and NFL Commissioner Roger Goodell wear Meta glasses before a Saints game in New Orleans on Oct. 5. Photo: Gerald Herbert/AP Meta is assembling a bipartisan team of Washington veterans as the tech giant looks to deepen its relationships with Democrats while retaining its standing with Republicans, Axios' Sara Fischer reports. 

 Why it matters: Mark Zuckerberg — the founder, chairman and CEO — has developed a close relationship with President Trump over the past few years, which has helped Meta navigate regulatory scrutiny of AI.

 In September, Zuckerberg and Nvidia founder and CEO Jensen Huang helped bring a slew of top AI executives to the White House to establish self-regulatory commitments . 🔎 Zuckerberg and Meta president and vice chairman Dina Powell McCormick met in August with the Democratic House Commission on Artificial Intelligence and the Innovation Economy at the invitation of Rep. Josh Gottheimer (D-N.J.), sources tell Axios.

 The executives discussed the company's AI strategy, including its infrastructure build-out and economic investment plans, with Gottheimer and other Democrats who co-chair the commission, including California Rep. Ted Lieu and North Carolina Rep. Valerie Foushee. Gottheimer, in a phone call with Axios yesterday, called the meeting "incredibly productive." He wanted to get the executives' perspectives as they try to put together a legislative framework for AI. 🫏 State of play: A new recruitment effort by Powell McCormick, a former bank executive and official in the first Trump administration, is underway, sources tell Axios.

 Michael Hacker, a longtime aide to House Democratic power broker Jim Clyburn, recently joined as a VP of compute initiatives. Nick Schmit, a former top aide to Biden Commerce Secretary Gina Raimondo, has joined the company as director of strategic partnership management. 🐘 Between the lines: Meta has also hired several former Trump administration officials to keep close ties to the White House.

 Josh Raffel, who worked with Powell McCormick during the first Trump administration, has joined as a VP of compute initiatives. Pat Trueman, a former senior official on Trump's 2024 presidential campaign, recently joined Meta's U.S. policy operation. Go deeper . 

 
 
