 6. ↩️ Young voters&#x27; U-turn 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Generation Lab/Axios. Chart: Avery Lotz/Axios In 2024, the Trump campaign made inroads with the youth vote by seizing on manosphere cultural stars to connect with young Americans: They voted Republican in higher-than-usual numbers.

 Two years later, President Trump's youth support has dropped, Axios' Avery Lotz and Margaret Talev write. 📊 In a new Generation Lab poll for Axios, 48% of 18-to-29-year-old, college-educated Democrats, 22% of independents and 6% of Republicans called Trump the biggest threat to America today.

 A New York Times/Siena poll of likely midterm voters published last week found that 7 in 10 young voters (ages 18-29) identified as or leaned toward Democrats — a 15-point swing from before the 2024 election. Keep reading . 

 
 
