 7. 📺 Where record ad money went 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 


 Data: AdImpact (as of Tuesday). Graphic: Jillian Vordick/The New York Times More than one-fourth of all the midterm ad spending has gone to just three races — the Senate races in Michigan, Ohio and Texas, the N.Y. Times' Jillian Vordick and Teddy Schleifer report . 

 All three states went for President Trump in 2024, and all three races are rated as toss-ups by the Cook Political Report. (The other Senate toss-ups are Alaska, Iowa, Kansas and Maine.) Republicans are spending $2.1 billion across all races, outspending Democrats, who are spending $1.8 billion.

 Senate races account for 60% of all ad spending up to the final week of midterm campaigning. 👀 NEW RECORD: This midterm cycle has broken the record for ad spending on any election, including presidential years. AdImpact says  total ad spending on the 2025-26 cycle crossed $11.6 billion, passing the record set in 2023-24. 

